  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill (it has `name`/`description` front matter), so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions` applies. Its `description` opens with \"Use when Habeas evidence needs creating or refreshing, or when `habeas coverage` or `habeas status` reports Habeas findings…, even if the user only says \\\"the habeas test is failing\\\"\". That states when to use the skill in terms of the user's task and situation. The closing sentence, \"If evidence went stale because code or requirements moved, use habeas-refactor first\", names another bundled skill (`assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md` exists). The requirement allows this where an agent could confuse the two skills. No violation match is listed, and I found no gap.",
